# Network tier

Narrative and code map: [docs/network-tier.md](../../docs/network-tier.md). Read it before changing this area.

## Must preserve

- **Product goal:** high-end experience (full WebPs, aerial cinema) when the connection allows it.
- **Resilience:** light path (`-light.webp`, static cinema, no MP4) must stay usable on constrained bandwidth / devices. Do not break it when polishing the full path.
- Session **`full` | `light`**. Runtime defaults unknown → light; `markLight()` locks; upgrade only via prove/`markFull()`. No site-wide `srcset` yet.
- Build: full WebP (1600) + `-light.webp` (800), q80; emit then prune around `vite build`.
- Cinema: never block the page; never autoplay with sound. Stall/timeout → light → static end poster.
- Keep tier/prove in `network-*.ts`; buffer/session in `ambient-video.ts`; cinema layout in `+page.svelte`.
- Update `ambient-video.test.ts`, `network-tier.test.ts`, `network-prove.test.ts` when tier, buffer, or control rules change.
